om/toronto-seniors-social-club/events/315396509/","description":"Thanksgiving Day - **MON, OCT 12/26 Departs:** York Mills Subway Station at 9:15 am / Islington at 10:00 am. Enjoy a delicious hot Turkey lunch at Mrs. Mitchell’s. Then, enjoy a train ride onboard the South Simcoe Railway. You’ll travel in restored 1920s coaches over the rails of a century-old branch line that once connected Hamilton with Barrie and Collingwood. Enjoy the sights and sounds of the vintage locomotive as you travel through the rolling countryside. The round trip from Tottenham to Beeton is highlighted by the Conductor’s friendly and informative commentary. Experience travel as our ancestors did, and learn about the history of the railways that made Canada what it is today! Before heading home, enjoy a “Taste and Shop” experience at Magnotta Winery, which includes 4 wine tastings and browsing in their gift shop. RTA: 6:30 p.m. RATE: $160.00.\n\n**RESERVE YOUR SEAT ON MARY MORTON TOURS BY booking** on-**line at ,** https://www.marymortontours.com/ **or CALL (416) 488-2674. LET THEM KNOW YOU ARE WITH CINDY STEVENS GROUP.** WHEN YOU HAVE BOOKED YOUR TICKET LET ME KNOW IN COMMENTS BELOW. : )","startDate":"2026-10-12T14:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Seniors Social Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-seniors-social-club/"},"performer":"Toronto Seniors Social Club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Make Lotions, Potions and Creams: Beginner's Workshop","url":"https://www.meetup.com/follow-your-bliss-yoga-tantra-life/events/316663901/","description":"Lotions, Potions & Creams I\n\nDread the feeling of dry, itchy skin? The obnoxious fragrances and unreadable ingredients of drug store moisturizing lotions? Want to moisturize and nourish your skin without feeling like you've been dunked in a tank of grease?\n\nCome learn to make your own lotions, for yourself, your family, and your clients. We'll use simple, natural, vegan ingredients like vegetable waxes and flower waters. You'll chose enhancing ingredients like essential oils, cocoa butter, shea butter, argan, tamanu, evening primrose, rosehip and calendula oil to meet individual skin needs.\n\nYou'll not only learn how to make a basic white lotion and basic white cream from scratch, but also how to protect yourself and your loved ones, no matter how young, from harmful sun rays, while still making and storing essential vitamin D by using natural ingredients like shea butter, cocoa butter, coconut and avocado oils.\n\nYou'll preserve with essential oils and grapefruit seed extract instead of harmful ingredients. We will create:\n\n• Basic White Cream and/or\n• Basic White Lotion\n• Cocoa Cream or\n• Shea Butter Cream\n• Your Very Own Custom Elemental Protection Lotion\n• Your Very Own Custom Specialty Cream (such as Anti Ageing, or Eczema, or Healing or? ...)\n\nFinally, you will package and label your creations in beautiful cobalt blue jars, metal and glass pump bottles.\n\nYou'll come away with the lotions, potions and creams you've made, and skills that can serve you for a lifetime for a fraction of the cost of a quality moisturizer!\n\nWhat I enjoyed about the Lotions and Creams course is that Tracey the instructor didn't just know how to make creams and lotions, she knew extensively the products we were working with to a point that she could make recommendations suited to the kind of cream/lotion you wanted to make and all the properties of those products at the drop of a hat. She is so knowledgeable.\n\nThe course taught me everything I needed to know about making lotions and creams and how to customize them to suit my customers needs and my own. She is truly in the right field of work. We laughed, we learned and we created not just lotions but memories.\n\nSincerely,\nStephanie Atwood, Oshawa Ontario, healer and co-owner of natural product company http://www.TranquilityMatters.ca\n\nThis is the PRE REQUISITE to Lotions II. Lotions II Advanced will take place Monday April 13th. Register & pre pay with a friend for both for a discount (see below). (http://www.TranquilityMatters.ca)\n\nVegan/ Hallal / Kosher / Gluten-free LUNCH and COFFEE TEA WATER are included. Please bring your reusable bottle or mug. Please don't bring throw away containers!\n\nRegister here: http://www.anarreshealth.ca/workshop/workshop-lotions-i","startDate":"2026-10-12T14:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Anarres Apothecary","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"749 Dovercourt Rd, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Follow Your Bliss: Yoga. Tantra. Life.","url":"https://www.meetup.com/follow-your-bliss-yoga-tantra-life/"},"performer":"Follow Your Bliss: Yoga. Tantra. Life."},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Beginner Drop-In Pickleball – $18/1.5hrs – Register to Secure Your Spot!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-miles-nadal-jcc-sports-and-recreation/events/316665380/","description":"🏓 **Registration & Payment (Required in Advance):**\nRSVP on Meetup does *not* guarantee your spot.\nTo play, you must register and pay in advance through our registration system.\n👉 **[Register online](https://app.amilia.com/store/en/miles-nadal-jcc/api/Activity/Detail?activityId=kLGNZre)**\n📞 Or call: 416-924-6211 ext. 0\n**Limited to 18 players.** Once full, no additional players will be admitted.\n\n***\n\n**Beginner Drop-In Pickleball at the Miles Nadal JCC**\nNew to pickleball? We’ve got the perfect session for you!\nJoin us for **Beginner Drop-In Pickleball** at the Miles Nadal JCC — a welcoming and supportive environment for those just getting started with the game. Whether you're still learning the rules or building confidence on the court, this is a great opportunity to play, practice, and meet fellow beginners.\n\n***\n\n🏓 **Event Details:**\n**Location:** 750 Spadina Ave. (enter through the Spadina doors)\n**Check-In:** Please check in with security and stop by the front desk upon arrival.\n\n***\n\n🏓 **What to Expect:**\n\n* Designed for **beginner-level players** with some familiarity with the rules and scoring\n* Equipment available: borrow paddles and balls with a $20 cash deposit + valid ID\n* Friendly rotations so everyone gets a chance to play\n* Supportive and inclusive environment — no pressure, just fun and learning!\n\n***\n\nCome ready to move, meet new people, and improve your game one rally at a time. We look forward to seeing you on the court!","startDate":"2026-10-12T15:45:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Miles Nadal JCC","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"750 Spadina Ave - M5S 2J2, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-miles-nadal-jcc-sports-and-recreation/"},"performer":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🍁 The Fall Colours of Brickworks (Thanksgiving Walk) 🍂","url":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/events/316545603/","description":"🍁 **The Fall Colours of Brickworks (Thanksgiving Walk)** 🍂\n\nCelebrate Thanksgiving with a scenic fall walk through Toronto’s ravines as we make our way to **Evergreen Brick Works**. Along the way, enjoy the crisp autumn air, brilliant fall colours, and a peaceful escape from the city.\n\nWe’ll spend about **30 minutes exploring the Brick Works**, taking in its history, trails, and unique setting before heading back through **Mount Pleasant Cemetery** — one of Toronto’s largest and oldest cemeteries, with plenty of history and beautiful seasonal scenery.\nFor those who’d like to keep the day going, we’ll finish with a cozy **Thanksgiving lunch at Swiss Chalet**.\n\nTheir seasonal special is expected to be around **$18.29 plus tax and tip** and includes stuffing, cranberry sauce, your choice of side, a roll, and a slice of pie — a pretty good way to finish a Thanksgiving walk! 🦃🥧\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n### Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** I will be standing outside of ST. CLAIR SUBWAT STATION right beside the McDonald wearing my Moose Hat. 🦌\n🕛 **Meetup Time:** 12:00pm\n**I will only wait 5 minutes.**\n💲 **Meetup Fee:** $5 cash 💵 or e-transfer 📲 to **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\n📍 **Ending Spot:** Swiss Chalet, a few blocks from the station.\n\nPlanning to join us for lunch? Please let me know so I can give Swiss Chalet a rough estimate of how many people to expect. They don’t take reservations, but I’d like to give them an approximate number so they can be prepared for our group.\n\n🍁 **Please note:** Swiss Chalet is a continuation of this event, not a separate event for anyone joining us for the walk. If you are attending the Brick Works walk **and** joining us for lunch at Swiss Chalet, you only pay the **$5 Meetup fee once**.\nIf you are **only joining us at Swiss Chalet** and are not attending the walk, please sign up for the separate Swiss Chalet event. The **$5 Meetup fee applies** to that event.\n\n***\n\n### What to Bring\n\n* Water\n* Good walking shoes 👟\n* A jacket or extra layer — fall weather can change quickly\n* Your camera or phone if you want to capture the colours! 📸\n\n***\n\n### More About the Brick Works 🧱\n\nFrom 1889 through the 1980s, the Don Valley Brick Works was one of Canada’s leading brickyards. In the 1990s, the former quarry was restored by the City of Toronto and the Toronto and Region Conservation Authority, transforming the site into the natural and cultural destination we know today.\nOpened to the public in 1996, Evergreen Brick Works now combines history, nature, wildlife, and trails in the heart of Toronto’s ravine system. In autumn, the surrounding landscape comes alive with reds, oranges, and golds, making it one of the city's great places to enjoy the fall colours.\n\n***\n\n✨ **Not sure yet? You can just show up on the day!**\n⚠️ **Sometimes things happen and I may need to cancel. Please watch for updates before heading out.**\n\n👤 **Organized by Mathew.**\nFor questions, post on the Meetup wall or email **[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**","startDate":"2026-10-12T16:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"McDonald's","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"11 St Clair Ave E, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/"},"performer":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Drop-In Pickleball (3.0+) – $18/1.5hrs – Register to Secure Your Spot!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-miles-nadal-jcc-sports-and-recreation/events/316666332/","description":"**🏓 Registration & Payment (Required in Advance):**\n**RSVP on Meetup does *not* reserve your spot.**\nTo participate in Drop-In Play, you must register and pay in advance via our registration system.\n👉 **[Register online](https://app.amilia.com/store/en/miles-nadal-jcc/api/Activity/Detail?activityId=yJJNJ6a)**\n📞 Or register by phone: 416-924-6211 ext. 0\nSpace is limited to **6 players** on a first-come, first-served basis. Once full, no additional participants can be accommodated.\n\\*\\*\\*\n**Drop-In Pickleball at the Miles Nadal JCC**\nCome play one of the fastest-growing sports in North America — right in the heart of the Annex!\nJoin us for friendly, active Pickleball at the Miles Nadal JCC, just steps from Spadina Station. It’s a great way to stay active, meet new people, and have some fun!\n\\*\\*\\*\n**🏓 Event Details:**\n**Location:** 750 Spadina Ave. (enter through the Spadina doors)\n**Check-In:** Stop by security and check in at the front desk when you arrive.\n\\*\\*\\*\n**🏓 Other Info:**\n\n* Paddles and balls are available for loan at the front desk with a **$20 cash deposit and valid ID**\n* This session is intended for **intermediate players and above** — participants should have a solid understanding of Pickleball rules, scoring, and gameplay, and be comfortable with consistent rallies and court positioning\n* Courts are rotated regularly so everyone gets a chance to play\n* Welcoming, inclusive environment\n\n\\*\\*\\*\nCome ready to rally, socialize, and have a great time on the court. We can’t wait to see you there!","startDate":"2026-10-12T17:15:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Miles Nadal JCC","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"750 Spadina Ave - M5S 2J2, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-miles-nadal-jcc-sports-and-recreation/"},"performer":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🍂 Thanksgiving International Potluck 🥧","url":"https://www.meetup.com/catholic-hang-out-social-group/events/316769583/","description":"You're invited to our Thanksgiving International Potluck! Join us for an afternoon of great food, wonderful company, and community. Let's celebrate gratitude together by sharing our favorite dishes from around the world.\n\nWhether you're bringing a traditional family recipe or a new favorite, we can't wait to share a meal with you.\n\n📅 Date: Saturday, October 12\n⏰ Time: 1:30 PM - 3:30 PM\n📍 Location: 879 St Clair Ave W\n\n🍽️ What to Bring:\nPlease bring a dish to share! To make sure we have a balanced meal, please mention in the comments what you plan to bring (appetizer, main, side, or dessert) so we can coordinate.\n\nCome hungry and ready to make new friends. RSVP today so we know how many to expect. See you there!","startDate":"2026-10-12T17:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"879 St Clair Ave W","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"879 St Clair Ave W, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Catholic Hang-out / Social Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/catholic-hang-out-social-group/"},"performer":"Catholic Hang-out / Social Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Rubber Stamp Making Workshop","url":"https://www.meetup.com/craft-hub-toronto/events/316778498/","description":"Design and carve 2 costum rubber stamps and take them home with an ink pad! Please register through this link: [https://www.zeffy.com/en-CA/ticketing/rubber-stamp-carving-workshop-thanksgiving](https://www.zeffy.com/en-CA/ticketing/rubber-stamp-carving-workshop-thanksgiving)","startDate":"2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"GlobalDWS","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"2, 68 Railside Rd, North York, ON M3A 1A3, Canada, toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Craft Hub Toronto: Woodcarving Workshops","url":"https://www.meetup.com/craft-hub-toronto/"},"performer":"Craft Hub Toronto: Woodcarving Workshops"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🦃✨ Thanksgiving @ Swiss Chalet ✨🍂","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316545601/","description":"🦃✨ **Thanksgiving @ Swiss Chalet** ✨🍂\n\nOkay, so it’s chicken and not turkey — but it comes with **all the trimmings of a Thanksgiving feast!** 🎉\nJoin me on Thanksgiving for a cozy meal at Swiss Chalet. You can order whatever you like from the menu, or opt for their **Festive Special** (starting at **$18.29 + tax & tip**, subject to change as we get closer).\n\n🍗 Quarter Chicken (dark meat, upgrade to white meat for +$2.00)\n🥔 Choice of side\n🥖 White or multigrain roll\n🍎 Stuffing & cranberry sauce\n🥧 A slice of pie (sometimes selections run out, so first come, first serve!)\nEveryone is responsible for their own meal.\n\n📋 **Full menu:** [Swiss Chalet Menu](https://www.swisschalet.com/en/menu.html?s=1225)\n\n### 🍁 Coming from the Brick Works Walk?\n\nThis is the **lunch-only event**. If you’re already joining me for the Thanksgiving walk at the Brick Works, **you do not need to sign up for this event or pay another $5 Meetup fee**. The lunch is a continuation of the walk.\nIf you’re **only joining us for lunch**, this is the event you should sign up for. The $5 Meetup fee applies.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n### Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Location:** Swiss Chalet at Yonge & St. Clair — northwest side of Yonge, just a block north of St. Clair.\n🕛 **Meetup Spot:** I’ll meet you outside wearing my **Moose Hat 🦌**. Please don’t go inside until I arrive so we can all sit together.\n💲 **Meetup Fee:** $5 cash 💵 or e-transfer 📲 to **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\n🕑 **Length:** About 2 hours, but you’re welcome to leave anytime.\n\n### ⚠️ A Quick Note About Seating\n\nSwiss Chalet does not take reservations, so I’ll give the restaurant a rough estimate of how many people to expect. **Please let me know if you’re planning to join us so I can give them the best number possible.**\n\nPlease **don’t call the restaurant** — they won’t know anything about this event. Message Mathew directly with any questions.\n\n✨ **Not sure yet? You can just show up on the day!**\n⚠️ Sometimes things happen and I may need to cancel — please keep an eye out for updates.\n\n👤 **Organized by Mathew.** For questions, post on the wall or email **[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**","startDate":"2026-10-12T19:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"1560 Yonge St","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto",